  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Watched Black Hole",
    "overview": "The background check is a black hole you can watch. Across the top, a dot-drawn, ray-traced accretion disk turns while UsageForge runs and hangs still when it is off, idle, hidden, or when the reader asks for reduced motion. Everything below sits on the same night ground and speaks the same grammar: dots. Usage meters are rows of lit dots, the day bar's track is a dot grid, mode choices carry little dot glyphs, status is one dot.\n\nLight comes from the disk. Its ember, gold and hot cream carry active state, selection and primary actions; the photon ring's ice blue carries focus, links and \"now\". Everything else is cool star dust on near-black navy. The panel is calm and dense enough to read at a glance, with no cards: parts sit directly on the ground, opened by hairlines.\n\nIt refuses the default dark dashboard: no neon accent, no glowing edges, no card grid, no glass.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Near-black navy ground with a faint 14px dot field that runs the whole page.",
      "Disk light (ember, gold, hot cream) means \"active / chosen\"; ring ice means \"focus / now / link\".",
      "Dots as the unit of every indicator.",
      "Hairline borders and tonal fills only; no cards, no glass.",
      "Jost for words, system mono for times and numbers.",
      "Soft 10px corners on containers, 7px on controls."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Disk Light Rule",
        "body": "Warm color means \"this is on or chosen\", nothing else. Disk gold, cream and ember never decorate idle surfaces, headings or borders at rest.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ring Rule",
        "body": "Ice blue is reserved for focus, \"now\" and inline links. It never fills a button or marks a selection.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Alarm Rule",
        "body": "Flare is the only error color and appears only when something is actually wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Instrument Numbers Rule",
        "body": "Any clock time, log line or model id is set in mono with tabular numerals; prose stays in Jost.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Axis-Only Caps Rule",
        "body": "Uppercase tracked text is for chart axis labels only. It never sits above a heading as a label.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Card Rule",
        "body": "Panels have no background, border box or shadow. A panel is opened by a top hairline (Line 2) and divided by section hairlines (Line).",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** build every indicator from dots: meters, tracks, status and mode glyphs.",
      "**Do** use disk gold for what is on or chosen and ring ice for focus, \"now\" and links.",
      "**Do** set times and numbers in mono with tabular numerals.",
      "**Do** separate parts with 1px hairlines on the void instead of cards.",
